# Generated, never hand-authored -- reformatting drifts it from its
# generator instead of the other way around. One glob covers every published
# fact-model schema (scripts/generate-json-schema.mjs's TARGETS list) so a
# new model's schema is excluded automatically, not by remembering to add a
# line here each time. benchmarks/history/*.json (moved from
# docs/benchmark-history/*.json) needs no separate entry -- it's already
# covered by the blanket `benchmarks` exclusion above.
schemas/*.schema.json

# Changesets-managed; reformatting past entries creates noise unrelated to
# the actual change.
CHANGELOG.md

# Lockfile -- npm owns its formatting.
package-lock.json

# Tooling-owned, never hand-formatted -- same rationale as eslint.config.js's own
# `.repo-contract` ignore entry. api-contract/: baseline.api.json/baseline.d.ts are hash-verified
# against baseline.meta.json (see internal-package-contract's own
# scripts/api-contract/baseline-store.ts) and current.* is regenerated every run --
# reformatting either corrupts the snapshot compatibility diffing depends on. exceptions/: the
# reviewed-exception registries. Matches internal-package-contract's own repo-contract's identical
# entry.
.repo-contract

# Generated by the shared benchmark contract (`npm run benchmark`); reformatting would drift it from its generator.
benchmarks/performance-runtime/results.json
benchmarks/performance-runtime/BENCHMARKS.md
benchmarks/performance-buildtime/results.json
benchmarks/performance-buildtime/BENCHMARKS.md
